// reserved-name-refused.maxtest — An author may not declare a reserved `__` name, and `test` must refuse it exactly as
// `build` does — even though half the staged file's bytes are this compiler's.
//
// ⛔⛔ **TWO SPAWNING TESTS LIVE HERE, AND THAT IS A CORRECTNESS RULE RATHER THAN AN EXCEPTION TO THE
// ONE-PER-FILE ONE.** Both name the SAME fixture, and `maxon test` shards by FILE and runs the shards
// CONCURRENTLY while every spawned run PURGES and re-stages `<fixture>/.maxon/test/staged/`. Split across
// two files they are two processes racing on one directory — MEASURED as exactly that: a flake that hit
// twice in ~27 runs, which is a 1-in-14 red on a gate with no diagnosis attached. In one file they are
// one process and run in order, so the race cannot happen.
//
// ⚠ Two spawns is ~2.6s of the 5s per-PROCESS deadline that `fixtures.maxtest`'s header prices. A
// THIRD here would be pushing it: give a new spawning case its own fixture and its own file, as every
// other case here does.

let ReservedNameCase = "reserved-name-refused"

test 'reserved-name-refused refuses an author declaring a __ name'
	checkFixture("reserved-name-refused")
end 'reserved-name-refused refuses an author declaring a __ name'

// `maxon test` compiles a staged copy under `<project>/.maxon/test/staged/`, and without
// `Compiler.StagedSourceOrigin` a diagnostic would name that copy. The fixture's `expected.txt`
// compares stdout while the diagnostic goes to stderr, so the assertion belongs here, where stderr
// is readable.
//
// The needle is the case directory immediately followed by the file name; the staged spelling
// separates those two with `/.maxon/test/staged/`, so no staged path can satisfy it. An assertion
// that the word `staged` is absent would restate `TestCommand.StagedTreeDirName` in a file that
// cannot import it, and would pass forever once that directory is renamed.
test 'a compile error names the author file, not the staged copy'
	let run = runFixture(ReservedNameCase)
	Expect.contains(run.stderr, needle: "{ReservedNameCase}{FilePath.separator()}sneaky.maxtest:", message: "a compile error under `{TestedCommandName}` must name the author's own file at the path they can open, not the staged copy the next run deletes. It said: {run.stderr}")
end 'a compile error names the author file, not the staged copy'
